From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sarol263@student.otago.ac.nz>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:59:18 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] Plutonium: agents drive windows and tabs

- T3's MCP server offers the Plutonium helper's native window tools
  (launch_app, snapshot_window, click_window, type_window, press_window,
  scroll_window, drag_window, ...) to every provider. The helper defines
  them (GET /v1/mcp/tools?set=windows) and runs them for the calling
  thread's tag (POST /v1/threads/<tag>/mcp/call). Tabs stay T3's preview
  tools. Claude no longer gets the helper's stdio MCP server as well.
- The desktop browser channel's `open` and `close`: a server tab no shell
  page shows is opened by the helper (tagged with its thread) and attached
  at once, instead of a 10 s wait and a headless tab; the helper closes it
  when its preview closes. A shell page that shows the thread adopts it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
